ace his journey to learn about her family history. Despite suffering from extreme disorientation and a lifetime of anxiety, she travels alone for the first time. Moving from Amsterdam to Lyon--relying on the marvels of GPS--she discovers family secrets and her own narrative as a second-generation Jewish Canadian. With vulnerability, humour, and wisdom, Lewis's memoir asks tough questions about her identity as a secular Jew, the accuracy of family stories, and the impact of the Holocaust on subsequent generations. How do immigrants weave their sense of identity into their chosen countries? Must we be able to locate ourselves within family and cultural geography to belong?\"--","publicationYear":2019,"displaySummary":"With vulnerability, humour, and wisdom, Lewis's memoir asks tough questions about her identity as a secular Jew, the accuracy of family stories, and the impact of the Holocaust on subsequent generations. How do immigrants weave their sense of identity into their chosen countries? Must we be able to locate ourselves within family and cultural geography to belong?\"--","primaryTopic":"Holocaust","subjectEvidence":{"primarySubject":"Travel & Place","confidence":"medium","method":"evidence_score","candidates":[{"subject":"Travel & Place","score":8,"evidenceCount":1}],"evidence":[{"source":"llm_classifier","rawLabel":"Travel & Place","mappedSubject":"Travel & Place","score":8,"confidence":"high","note":"The book focuses on travel writing and place-based narratives, while also reflecting on cultural experiences and societal themes related to travel.","id":"subject-evidence-book-tiny-lights-for-travellers-naomi-k-lewis-1"},{"source":"open_library","scheme":"open_library_subject","rawLabel":"Canada, biography","mappedSubject":"Biography","score":6,"confidence":"high","sourceId":"source-open-library-summary-tiny-lights-for-travellers-naomi-k-lewis","id":"subject-evidence-book-tiny-lights-for-travellers-naomi-k-lewis-4"},{"source":"open_library","scheme":"open_lib